Subject: [PATCH 7/8] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: add Realme GT7 Pro gauge, 18W PD, and OTG 5V boost

- Initialize battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh on SM8350/SM8550 variants
  so charge_full and charge_full_design are reported instead of -ENODATA
- Fix supplied_to battery name ("qcom-battmgr-bat") and notify both USB and
  battery power supplies on USB/OEM GLINK notifications (0x50..0x7f)
- Read Oplus ADSP OEM_READ_BUFFER (opcode 0x10000) to expose real hardware
  fuel-gauge SOH, cycle count, and 2S dual-cell voltages on Realme GT7 Pro
  (2S x 3250 mAh = 6500 mAh / ~25.2 Wh pack), with standard Linux ABI
  current_now sign and real V*I pack power_now
- Negotiate safe 9V / 2A (18W) USB-PD buck charging via ADSP when a PD/PPS
  adapter is connected, with automatic 5V thermal/SOC step-down (>=45C or >=95%)
- Enable Oplus Type-C OTG CC DRP detection (OEM_PROP_OTG_SWITCH 0x0d = 1)
  and drive automatic cold-socket 5V VBUS boost (OEM_PROP_OTG_BOOST 0x13,
  1500mA current limit 0x3b) via usb_register_notify() on xHCI host bus
  add/remove so external USB drives and peripherals power on automatically
